<section class="higa-story section" id="what-is-higa">
  <div class="shell higa-grid">
    <img
      src="/assets/images/higa-amulet.jpg"
      alt="The Higa amulet"
      width="1154"
      height="1572"
      loading="lazy"
      class="reveal"
    />
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="kicker">The symbol</p>
      <h2>What is<br /><span>Higa?</span></h2>
      <p>
        The Higa amulet, also known as the Mano Figa, is a protective charm shaped like a closed fist. For centuries, people have worn it to ward off the evil eye.
      </p>
      <p>
        Medieval pilgrims often carried the Higa along the Camino de Santiago for spiritual protection. For women, it also came to represent empowerment and a connection to feminine spiritual strength.
      </p>
      <p>
        We chose this amulet to honour its history and its enduring meaning for pilgrims and women focused on cultivating inner strength and perseverance.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .higa-story {
    color: white;
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6e168f, #2a093f);
  }

  .higa-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.75fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(50px, 9vw, 130px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .higa-grid > img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 690px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 140px 4px 4px;
  }

  .higa-grid .kicker {
    color: var(--color-pink-soft);
  }

  .higa-grid p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .higa-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .higa-grid > img {
      max-height: 620px;
      width: min(100%, 580px);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .higa-grid > img {
      max-height: 540px;
      border-radius: 90px 4px 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
